WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:01.568
Here in Dnipro, Garrison Foster.

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:02.969
He was in the infantry with the U.S.

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:04.571
Marine Corps for six years

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:05.505
now fighting alongside

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:06.806
Ukrainian forces and Garrison.

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:07.640
I'm glad to see you.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:08.274
Obviously, a,

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:08.775
you know, a

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:11.144
dark a dark, chilly, wet night here

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:12.746
in dark brown.

00:00:12.746 --> 00:00:13.646
So you're

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:15.715
just obviously off the front lines

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:16.883
nearby as well.

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:18.351
And you've shared some GoPro footage

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:18.618
sort of thing.

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:18.952
You know,

00:00:18.952 --> 00:00:19.252
when you

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:20.553
when you're in on your mask

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:21.955
wearing your chest,

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:22.555
that sort of shows

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:23.256
your perspective as you're

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:24.724
gathering intelligence

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:27.694
to try to target Russian Russian forces.

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:29.796
I know you've been here since April

00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:30.663
of last year.

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:31.064
Mm hmm.

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:32.632
And a brief visit home

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:34.734
for the birth of your son. Yes.

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:36.102
You're putting your life in danger

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:37.470
to help another country.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.972
I think everybody wants to understand

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:39.606
what drives you.

00:00:39.606 --> 00:00:41.574
What drives you to do it, Garrison?

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:43.043
Well, part of it is

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:43.443
a lot of people

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:44.177
aren't aware of this,

00:00:44.177 --> 00:00:46.046
but the Ukrainians sent soldiers

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:48.214
to Afghanistan after nine 11.

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:50.150
They were part of the forces

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:50.550
that were there,

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.785
and they were under no obligation

00:00:51.785 --> 00:00:52.852
to do so.

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:54.421
And so to me, it's,

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:54.854
you know,

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:57.023
they came to us in our time of need,

00:00:57.023 --> 00:00:58.091
and I see no reason

00:00:58.091 --> 00:00:58.892
not to go to them in

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:01.261
their time of need as well.

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:02.462
You know,

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:04.564
this is a very resource dense area.

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:05.298
I don't want Russia

00:01:05.298 --> 00:01:06.533
to get a hold of those resources

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:07.133
and leverage

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:08.668
that to kind of destabilize

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:10.804
the world and, you know, create more war.

00:01:11.438 --> 00:01:12.505
So you've made

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:13.940
this great personal sacrifice.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:14.407
I want to show

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:15.075
some of the things

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:15.942
that you've experienced

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:16.676
that you're willing to share.

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:18.478
This is a really intense confrontation.

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:19.646
That you had with Russian forces

00:01:19.646 --> 00:01:20.880
recently, just a few weeks ago in the.

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:23.349
You came under fire

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:24.851
and you had to retreat.

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:26.686
And I just want to play that part

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:28.054
so people can actually see a little bit

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:29.255
you know, get a sense of what

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:30.890
it's like in those moments. Just listen.

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:31.958
Sure. Sure.

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:35.495
I think we're pulling back

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:39.899
we're moving

00:01:45.472 --> 00:01:47.373
I don't remember the minute

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:53.012
that was closest

00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:56.616
This is not a good spot to be, guys.

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:57.951
We got to move

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:04.357
get some counter battery up or something,

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:05.859
like you can't feel

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:08.628
okay through here.

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:11.531
Go, go, go, go, go, go.

00:02:35.188 --> 00:02:36.623
Bunker, bunker.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.762
Inside the so called

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:45.698
the ammo room.

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:47.066
Getting further

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:51.304
So watching

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:52.539
that is just give people

00:02:52.539 --> 00:02:54.541
a sense of that one moment.

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:55.608
What's been the hardest part

00:02:55.608 --> 00:02:57.677
of the counter-offensive so far?

00:02:57.677 --> 00:02:58.845
Well, right now

00:02:58.845 --> 00:03:00.246
we are conducting probing attacks

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:01.781
because we need to figure out

00:03:01.781 --> 00:03:03.449
where the weak spots are.

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:04.284
We need to figure out where

00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:05.485
the strong points are.

00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:06.052
We need to figure out

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:07.220
what to do about both of those

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:09.255
and how to make it work together.

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:10.223
There's been a lot of time

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:11.291
since the last offensive.

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:13.426
So the Russians are very, very dug in

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.562
entrenched positions.

00:03:15.562 --> 00:03:16.696
Lots of money. Yes.

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:19.299
And in order to dislodge them, you know,

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:20.767
sometimes the artillery won't do it

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:22.101
because the bunkers they have,

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:23.703
the artillery just can't penetrate.

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:26.139
And so we have to physically go up there

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:27.840
and try and dislodge them.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:28.741
And you were doing that

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:29.676
in one of these videos.

00:03:29.676 --> 00:03:30.276
You were trying to

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:30.977
to basically

00:03:30.977 --> 00:03:33.346
sneak up on a Russian position.

00:03:33.346 --> 00:03:35.915
And they saw you and they saw you

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:37.383
from the air.

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:37.784
Yeah.

00:03:37.784 --> 00:03:39.185
Tell me about what we're looking at.

00:03:39.185 --> 00:03:40.053
Yeah.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:41.221
Drones, these

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:42.889
these small commercially available

00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:45.692
drones are a big problem.

00:03:45.692 --> 00:03:46.459
It's good for us

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:47.493
because the Ukrainians

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:48.328
have a lot more of them.

00:03:48.328 --> 00:03:50.163
The ones they have are

00:03:50.163 --> 00:03:50.964
a lot more capable.

00:03:50.964 --> 00:03:53.132
But they they happened to see us.

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:54.100
They weren't even looking,

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:55.001
you know, in our area.

00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:56.002
They just turned

00:03:56.002 --> 00:03:56.970
and happened to see us

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:58.638
and then basically set up

00:03:58.638 --> 00:04:00.506
an ambush for us

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:01.174
while we were in the middle

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:02.308
of a minefield

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:03.643
approaching their position.

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:05.011
So it's that's

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:06.279
obviously a

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:07.380
continual problem,

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:08.248
but it's something we deal

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:10.116
with regularly now, so.

00:04:10.116 --> 00:04:12.385
And do you feel progress?

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:13.286
We hear the optimism

00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:14.220
we just heard from those

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:14.921
Ukrainian troops.

00:04:14.921 --> 00:04:16.089
They're about to go right back in. Right.

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:16.623
A few miles away.

00:04:16.623 --> 00:04:18.057
Do they're trying to go back in.

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:19.158
Is that the same optimism

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:21.160
that that you hear from the Ukrainians

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:21.961
that you feel?

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:23.997
Yes, absolutely. Absolutely.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:26.699
We have a very high degree of freedom

00:04:26.699 --> 00:04:27.900
within our area of operations.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:28.568
We're not just

00:04:29.636 --> 00:04:31.537
in one specific spot.

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:32.839
We kind of bounce around that area.

00:04:32.839 --> 00:04:33.573
And so we get to talk

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:34.507
to a lot of different units

00:04:34.507 --> 00:04:36.142
and they're there

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:37.710
Their morale is extremely high.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:38.778
And at the same time,

00:04:38.778 --> 00:04:39.812
there are Russians

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:41.147
who are in the middle of the day

00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:42.415
leaving their their gear

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:44.150
and equipment in their positions,

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:45.785
walking to the Ukrainian positions

00:04:45.785 --> 00:04:46.619
with their hands up

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:47.987
and basically saying that they're done.

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:49.722
They don't want to fight anymore. Hmm.

00:04:49.722 --> 00:04:50.423
It happened.

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:50.623
Yeah,

00:04:50.623 --> 00:04:52.091
it happened about four weeks ago

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:52.759
to a position

00:04:52.759 --> 00:04:54.661
that was directly next to us.

00:04:54.661 --> 00:04:56.863
The Russian soldiers just walked over

00:04:56.863 --> 00:04:57.730
to the Ukrainians.

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:59.432
And, you know, they're like, we're done.

00:04:59.432 --> 00:05:00.600
Please give us food and water

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:01.634
and we'd

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:02.435
rather be a prisoner

00:05:02.435 --> 00:05:04.137
than continue fighting.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:05.938
Garrison, thank you. Very much.

00:05:05.938 --> 00:05:06.639
I appreciate it.

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:07.473
And intervention understand

00:05:07.473 --> 00:05:08.041
obviously garrisons

00:05:08.041 --> 00:05:09.309
operating on frontlines right near here.

00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:09.876
And we very much

00:05:09.876 --> 00:05:10.810
appreciate your being here

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:11.644
with us tonight.

00:05:11.644 --> 00:05:12.578
Thank you for having me on.

